  "requirements": [
    "One canonical registry supplies prelude, type resolution, ownership, Copy/Send, and drop facts.",
    "Aliases share one canonical identity; spelling alone never grants identity.",
    "Generic arity is checked before backend lowering.",
    "Option and Result destruction visits only the active variant exactly once.",
    "Copy and Send are recursively derived from all contained payloads.",
    "Borrowed views cannot escape, become owned, or cross actor boundaries by name alone.",
    "Allocator-dependent types fail in core-only profiles before artifact emission.",
    "Unsupported backend lowering fails closed rather than silently using host collections.",
    "Active sums destroy only their active payload; arrays/tuples/pairs destroy all initialized members; owned containers destroy backing storage and initialized elements."
  ],
